{
 "result": "maze.py is a pure-Python BFS. It reads the grid as bytes into a padded bytearray (sentinel '#' border, so no bounds checks), finds S and E by buffer.find, and expands frontier by level using index offsets (-1, +1, -W, +W) on a 'seen' bytearray. It prints the depth at E, or -1 if unreachable. It matches all three public samples (2008, -1, 78) and was accepted by assay at baseline 3.53529 (noise 3.7%). I stopped here because further speedups would need to beat that baseline by more than 3.7%, and I have no concrete optimisation that clearly does so for the cost.",
